     [38;5;246mvalidation.js uses export; app.js imports it via <script type="module">. Real module boundary, no bundler, but the
[39m     [38;5;246mpage must be served over http rather than opened from disk.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Plain script + global
     [38;5;246mvalidation.js exposes a single global, loaded by a second <script> tag before app.js. Zero tooling, file:// keeps [39m
     [38;5;246mworking, at the cost of a global.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m CommonJS under src/
     [38;5;246mMatches src/utils.js and is directly testable in Node, but needs a bundler or a dual-export shim for the browser to
